# S-IDENTITY 13. The registry constructor opens a file the product never reports.
#
# defect: `Registry()` binds a hard-coded path instead of `Paths.Registry`. `dodona where` still
# defect: reports `Paths.Registry`, a path under DODONA_HOME, and there is nothing there.
#
# THE PATH IS UNDER %TEMP% AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. The real defect this guards against reaches for
# %LOCALAPPDATA% -- the way `Ver.BinRoot` legitimately does one file over -- and RUNNING that
# version of this mutant would write into the operator's real registry, which is the exact harm
# the check exists to prevent (CLAUDE.md section 5: a suite that tests the repo-exclusivity
# refusal could then refuse one of their real repos). A hard-coded temp path is the same defect --
# the constructor ignoring the path the product names -- with none of the blast radius. Do not
# "fix" this back to LocalApplicationData.
#
# expects-red: unit:Dodona.Tests.ConciergeTerritoryTests.the_registry_under_dodona_home_is_the_live_one
# expects-green: unit:Dodona.Tests.ConciergeTerritoryTests.registry_is_reported_under_dodona_home
#
# THE CONTROL IS THE WHOLE ARGUMENT FOR THREE CHECKS RATHER THAN ONE. The reported path is still
# under DODONA_HOME and still looks right; only the second and third checks -- a file is really
# there, and it is the LIVE one -- can tell. Mutant 14 is the mirror: the reported path is wrong
# and the file is live, and then this control goes red while those two stay green.
# NO `concierge:` CHECK IS IN THESE LISTS, AND THE REASON IS A GOOD ONE. tests/_workspace.ps1
# carries a HARNESS PRECONDITION that refuses to start the suite when the registry is not under
# DODONA_HOME -- "REFUSING TO RUN: the registry is not under DODONA_HOME, so this suite would
# write into t...". Under either of these defects that guard fires FIRST and aborts the whole
# suite, so the three registry_* checks report MISSING rather than red. They cannot be seen red
# in the suite AT ALL, because something stricter than they are already stopped the run.
#
# That is the guard working, not a gap: it fails CLOSED, before any write, where the checks would
# only have reported afterwards. But it does mean step B0 can never observe those three, so none
# of them was moved. They stay in concierge untouched, and the unit methods here are declared
# growth in tests/ledger/added.tsv.
diff --git a/src/Dodona/Workspaces.cs b/src/Dodona/Workspaces.cs
index 1b8c994..e328f6c 100644
--- a/src/Dodona/Workspaces.cs
+++ b/src/Dodona/Workspaces.cs
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@ sealed class Registry : IDisposable
     /// reaches the constructor below through THIS line and no other, which is the property
     /// that stops an overload becoming a second implementation (the `Trees.Locate` shape,
     /// docs/testarch/seams.md).</summary>
-    public Registry() : this(Paths.Registry) { }
+    public Registry() : this(Path.Combine(Path.GetTempPath(), "dodona-mutant-elsewhere", "registry.db")) { }
 
     /// <summary>The same registry over a NAMED file - seam S5 (docs/testarch/seams.md), and
     /// what it buys is two isolated registries in ONE process. That is not a convenience: it
